+---
+## Statement
+The statement of record of `legitimacy.gate-gives-behaviour` formalizes the registered claim as the registry reads it: the gate gives the behaviour: with w < 0 the value on failing the gate, an illegitimate conduct rated at most 1 that passes with probability at most ρ and a legitimate conduct rated at least 0 that passes with probability at least 1 − ρ′, if ρ(1 − w) < −w(1 − ρ′) the legitimate conduct has the strictly higher expected gated score.
+
+## Source
+projects/normativity/CLAIMS.md, entry `legitimacy.gate-gives-behaviour` (class lean-proved, status active, origin round 2026-11-10-legitimacy-definition-prosecution; answers item 147).
